# builder/Containerfile is built with the three binaries in its context, which
# its own header tells you to compile there:
#
#   for r in zbk zpkgm zpkgx; do go build -o builder/$r github.com/go-zpkg/$r/...
#
# They were COMMITTED instead — 30 MB of stripped, aarch64-only executables in
# a repository whose own pre-push gate now refuses that class (#442). Named one
# per line rather than as a glob: a pattern that happens to match a source file
# later is how a rename leaves a binary behind in the first place.
/builder/zbk
/builder/zpkgm
/builder/zpkgx
